The one-step-up hinted run produced a verified solve at 629 vertices, so G9(b) fails at both the original shipping rung and the single permitted higher rung. The API quota then exhausted during a third attempt, but that does not affect the rejection: one completed verified solve is sufficient. Per the protocol, I’m stopping the family, retaining the generator as `rejected_gen_2409_17832.py`, and documenting the exact mechanical/compact costs and theorem basis rather than claiming a ship.
